:: Rehearsal [event sister_quest] {"position":"5150,1775","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Rehearsal" (sister_rehearsal), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 6.8c. Optional: only if I offered them to $supplier.callName
   ($flags.supplierOffered). The evening before the last night, the meeting room, device off: the Catalyst stays in my
   drawer and she doesn't ask for it. I play the supplier. Where to sit, how to laugh, when to let a hand stay, how to say
   no so it sounds like later. Halfway through she understands what she's being prepared for and asks: "Will you be
   there?" "Outside." "Then I can do it." We run it once more from the top, and she's good, which is the worst part.
   The mirror of the rooftop: there she waited for my signal, here she learns to do it without one. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silent>>
I've set the meeting room up like a club booth. Two chairs pushed together on one side of the table, a bottle of wine I won't open, two glasses, the lights turned down to the dimmest setting the dimmer allows. It looks less like a club than like a very sad date. It'll do.

She comes in at seven in the dress I told her to wear tomorrow, so she can practice walking in it, and stops in the doorway when she sees the room.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Either this is the world's most depressing candlelit dinner, or we're doing a drill." },
{ who: $player, text: "A drill. Tomorrow night you're a hostess again. A private club, an important client. I want you ready." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Like the rooftop?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Like the rooftop. A little more." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She doesn't ask what "a little more" means. She sets her purse down, smooths the dress, and sits where I point.

The Catalyst is in my desk drawer. I don't take it out. She doesn't look for it.

<<linkreplace "Play the client">>
I sit down next to her, close, closer than I'd sit to anyone at a business dinner, and put my arm along the back of her chair. I make my voice slower, softer, the way $supplier.callName's sounded on the phone.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "So you're the famous hostess. They told me you were charming. They didn't say beautiful." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Oh my God. Is this what he's like?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Stay in it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Sorry. Sorry. Okay." },
{ text: "She takes a breath, and her face changes. The smile comes up, bright and easy, the rooftop smile." },
{ who: $sister, text: "They told me you were difficult. Nobody said you were funny." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's good. It's very good. I keep going.

I teach her where to sit: always with the client between her and the room, so he feels like he's got her to himself. How to laugh: not at the joke, at him, a little before the punch line, so he thinks he's even funnier than he is. How to keep a glass full without seeming to. How to say no.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "He'll ask you to stay after. He'll ask you to come to the back. You don't say no. You say 'not yet', and you touch his arm when you say it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Not yet." },
{ who: $player, text: "And you smile like you mean later." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Not yet." },
{ text: "She does it, and touches my arm, and smiles. It's perfect. It's the most dangerous thing I've ever seen her do." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "His hand">>
I put my hand on her knee. The way he'll do it, probably: casually, while making a point about something else, and leaving it there to see what happens.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "If he does this?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Then I... I let it stay?" },
{ who: $player, text: "For as long as he's spending money. He'll be spending a lot." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She looks down at my hand on her knee. Then she looks at the two glasses, and the bottle, and the dim lights, and the way I've pushed the chairs together, and I watch her put it together, piece by piece, the way she puts together a proof in calculus. She's not stupid. She's never been stupid. She just used to not have the pieces.

Her smile goes away.

<<linkreplace "Wait">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "This isn't like the rooftop." },
{ who: $player, text: "No." },
{ who: $sister, text: "This is... the back room. And not yet. And later." },
{ text: "She isn't crying. She's very quiet and very still, with my hand still on her knee, and she doesn't move it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Will you be there?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<if $flags.retailIntro === "sister">>On the rooftop I was across the terrace the whole time, and she watched me for the signal. Tomorrow there won't be a terrace.<</if>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Outside." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She thinks about it. I can see her thinking about it, turning the word over, the way she turned over the word ours in this same room, months ago, checking it for cracks.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Outside. Okay." },
{ text: "She takes a long breath, and lets it out." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Then I can do it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "From the top">>
We run it again from the top, all of it: the door and the coat, the walk to the booth, the joke and the laugh a little before the punch line, the hand on the knee, the glass she keeps full without seeming to, the back room, not yet, the touch on the arm.

She's good. She's better than good. She doesn't look at me once for a signal, because tomorrow there won't be one, and she's already learned to do it without.

That's the worst part. I know it's the worst part. I make her run it one more time anyway, and she does, perfectly, and at the end she gives me the not-yet smile, and I can't tell if it's for the client or for me.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Was that good?" },
{ who: $player, text: "That was perfect." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay. Good." },
{ text: "She stands up, smooths the dress, picks up her purse. At the door she stops with her hand on the frame, the way she did after the first meeting in this room, when she told me I was kind of good at the boss thing." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You'll be right outside." },
{ who: $player, text: "Right outside." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She goes. I sit in the dim meeting room for a while with the unopened bottle and the two clean glasses, and then I turn the lights back up and push the chairs back where they belong, so tomorrow nobody will know.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterExhibition" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "SisterResistance" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 3>>
<<Feel $sister "player" -1>>
<<ProfileLog $sister "Rehearsal" "The evening before $supplier.callName's club, I rehearsed it with her in the meeting room, with the device in my drawer. I played him. Halfway through she understood what she was being prepared for and asked if I'd be there. I said outside. She said then she could do it. We ran it again, and she was perfect.">>
